    "created_at": "2017-02-15T16:36:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-15T16:36:36Z",
    "body": "The minimum guarantees all implementations give you are pretty small: the only security-checked cross-origin anything in some implementations are Window and Location.  I would probably be fine with the spec requiring security checks there and allowing them in other cross-origin situations...\r\n\r\n> Absent of that, at least capturing what one implementation does would still be better imo.\r\n\r\nI think in cases when there is fundamental disagreement like that, the best a spec can do is be honest about what behaviors people can expect and explicitly leave cases that are not agreed on as undefined in the spec or so.  Or defined with SHOULD/MAY instead of MUST.",
